WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:07.490 --> 00:00:10.690
Transylvania is like CATALONIA with vampires.

00:00:10.690 --> 00:00:12.240
Yep, you heard that right.

00:00:12.240 --> 00:00:16.660
The land where Dracula was born is also the
place of one of the most significant separatists

00:00:16.660 --> 00:00:19.100
conflicts in all of Europe.

00:00:19.100 --> 00:00:20.100
In other words…

00:00:20.100 --> 00:00:24.600
Transylvania is the perfect place to make
a VisualPolitik Halloween special.

00:00:24.600 --> 00:00:25.600
And…

00:00:25.600 --> 00:00:30.060
yes, I know what you are thinking.

00:00:30.060 --> 00:00:32.750
We read your comments and we know you want
a video about Catalonia...

00:00:32.750 --> 00:00:33.870
And I’ll tell you what!

00:00:33.870 --> 00:00:40.110
We are going make it, it’s just big, and
it’s complicated, and I promise it will

00:00:40.110 --> 00:00:41.160
be worth the wait…

00:00:41.160 --> 00:00:46.339
For now, let’s get back to Transylvania,
a historical region situated in the centre

00:00:46.339 --> 00:00:47.780
of Romania.

00:00:47.780 --> 00:00:51.900
Despite being in this country, 20% of its
population doesn’t even speak Romanian.

00:00:51.900 --> 00:00:58.530
Instead, Hungarian is their mother language.

00:00:58.530 --> 00:01:02.989
In some areas, the number of Hungarian-speaking
people rises to 80%.

00:01:02.989 --> 00:01:06.799
This area where the Hungarians are the majority
is called as SZEKELY LAND.

00:01:06.799 --> 00:01:11.520
Almost every year you can see massive protests
of Szekelies demanding more autonomy for their

00:01:11.520 --> 00:01:12.520
territory.

00:01:12.520 --> 00:01:16.310
These demonstrations are celebrated in the
main cities of Transylvania as well as Bucharest,

00:01:16.310 --> 00:01:19.470
the Romanian capital, and Budapest, the Hungarian
capital.

00:01:19.470 --> 00:01:23.140
But wait a minute because things are far more
complicated that they seem!

00:01:23.140 --> 00:01:26.020
In fact, Szekelys don’t want to have their
own country.

00:01:26.020 --> 00:01:31.530
Instead, they want to become a special region
inside of Romania, with a very specific fiscal

00:01:31.530 --> 00:01:32.530
system.

00:01:32.530 --> 00:01:33.829
So the question here is…

00:01:33.829 --> 00:01:36.619
Why does this cause so many problems for Romania?

00:01:36.619 --> 00:01:40.869
Why are these demands causing such a significant
diplomatic conflict?

00:01:40.869 --> 00:01:43.009
And more importantly…

00:01:43.009 --> 00:01:45.439
What does the Hungarian government have to
do with this?

00:01:45.439 --> 00:01:49.450
Well, today we are going to answer all of
these questions.

00:01:49.450 --> 00:01:58.100
But before we do that let’s take a look
at the history.

00:01:58.100 --> 00:01:59.100
HAIRY TONGUES

00:01:59.100 --> 00:02:03.280
For centuries, Transylvania was part of the
Kingdom of Hungary.

00:02:03.280 --> 00:02:05.789
Back then, Romania wasn’t even a country.

00:02:05.789 --> 00:02:10.630
The upper classes and the aristocracy spoke
Hungarian and Romanian was the language spoken

00:02:10.630 --> 00:02:11.709
by the peasants.

00:02:11.709 --> 00:02:18.090
At some points in history, Romanian speakers
were even prosecuted by the authorities.

00:02:18.090 --> 00:02:20.080
We call this process the MAGYARIZATION.

00:02:20.080 --> 00:02:25.360
Basically, the Hungarian rulers wanted to
impose their culture at any cost.

00:02:25.360 --> 00:02:29.280
To those aristocrats, Romanians were sort
of hillbillies who had a special love for

00:02:29.280 --> 00:02:32.370
stealing things and a bad sense of personal
hygiene...

00:02:32.370 --> 00:02:34.640
In fact, there was even a term to refer these
Romanians...

00:02:34.640 --> 00:02:44.730
They were called Szőrös nyelvu which, literally
means, ‘with a hairy tongue’.

00:02:44.730 --> 00:02:48.480
During the 19th century, the Government closed
Romanian speaking newspapers and they even

00:02:48.480 --> 00:02:53.230
forced a lot of citizens to change their Romanian
name to a Hungarian one.

00:02:53.230 --> 00:02:56.090
Nonetheless, things changed after the end
of World War I.

00:02:56.090 --> 00:02:58.720
The Austro-Hungarian empire lost the war.

00:02:58.720 --> 00:03:02.020
And one of the things that happens when you
lose a war is that you usually lose parts

00:03:02.020 --> 00:03:03.260
of your territory too.

00:03:03.260 --> 00:03:07.510
One of those parts was Transylvania, which
was incorporated into Romania.

00:03:07.510 --> 00:03:12.680
Suddenly, those peasants that were oppressed
by the Hungarian nobility had power.

00:03:12.680 --> 00:03:16.080
And, well, they wanted revenge.

00:03:16.080 --> 00:03:19.500
This is how the first attempts to destroy
the Hungarian culture started.

00:03:19.500 --> 00:03:28.890
And oh boy, it 
was not an easy job…

00:03:28.890 --> 00:03:34.240
Don’t forget that, despite being part of
Romania, Transylvania was the home of over

00:03:34.240 --> 00:03:36.920
1 million Hungarian speaking people.

00:03:36.920 --> 00:03:41.510
These were called the SZEKELIS and for generations
have been speaking the language of ISTVAN

00:03:41.510 --> 00:03:42.510
ORKENY.

00:03:42.510 --> 00:03:49.380
But things got really a lot uglier during
World War II.

00:03:49.380 --> 00:03:52.661
Hungary once again chose the wrong side to
ally with.

00:03:52.661 --> 00:03:56.790
With Hitler’s help, they took back their
former territories and struck back against

00:03:56.790 --> 00:04:00.210
those who wanted to erase Hungarian culture
in the country.

00:04:00.210 --> 00:04:03.730
As you can imagine, this helped to make the
Romanians even more angry.

00:04:03.730 --> 00:04:08.130
Then, in 1945, the Germans lost the war.

00:04:08.130 --> 00:04:11.140
That included their allies and, of course,
the Hungarians.

00:04:11.140 --> 00:04:16.380
So Romania, with a brand new communist government
took Transylvania back.

00:04:16.380 --> 00:04:21.660
This time, with an even bigger taste for a
payback.

00:04:21.660 --> 00:04:27.830
Maybe you remember this other video where
I told you about the dictatorship of Nicolae

00:04:27.830 --> 00:04:28.960
Ceausescu?

00:04:28.960 --> 00:04:33.110
If you have seen it, you already know the
Communist Romania was the closest thing to

00:04:33.110 --> 00:04:34.800
a European North Korea.

00:04:34.800 --> 00:04:40.490
1 out of 30 Romanians were part of the political
police, and they prosecuted not only those

00:04:40.490 --> 00:04:44.740
who opposed the government, but even those
who dared to speak Hungarian.

00:04:44.740 --> 00:04:49.930
From one day to the other, Ceaucescu closed
newspapers and forced those Szekelys to speak

00:04:49.930 --> 00:04:54.749
Romanian even in their own homes.

00:04:54.749 --> 00:05:01.550
Magyarization, bad as it was, forced a few
Romanians to change their names.

00:05:01.550 --> 00:05:05.650
Romanization was the same sort of thing, just
on a way bigger scale.

00:05:05.650 --> 00:05:09.560
But hold on a minute because it doesn’t
stop here!

00:05:09.560 --> 00:05:14.561
On their path to destroy even the last resemblance
of Hungarian culture, the Romanian Communist

00:05:14.561 --> 00:05:19.699
Party forced thousands of citizens to set
in the Hungarian speaking territories.

00:05:19.699 --> 00:05:24.580
This way, Hungarian speaking became a small
minority in cities like ORADEA or SATU MARE.

00:05:24.580 --> 00:05:28.949
Basically, the whole area that borders with
Hungary became a Romanian majority region.

00:05:28.949 --> 00:05:33.849
Nonetheless, there is a region that managed
to keep their language and traditions in tact,

00:05:33.849 --> 00:05:39.889
and that is the so-called SZEKELY LAND.

00:05:39.889 --> 00:05:43.050
ROMANIA STEALS FROM US!

00:05:43.050 --> 00:05:47.499
In 1991, Romania passed their brand new democratic
constitution.

00:05:47.499 --> 00:05:50.340
This constitution recognized the right to
speak Hungarian.

00:05:50.340 --> 00:05:54.699
But, as you can imagine, after decades of
hate against Budapest, those szekelys were

00:05:54.699 --> 00:05:56.760
far from happy.

00:05:56.760 --> 00:06:05.479
Think about it, fiscally, Romania is a very
centralized country.

00:06:05.479 --> 00:06:10.050
Almost all the taxes are collected by the
central government and then, they share that

00:06:10.050 --> 00:06:13.340
money among the regions, with a focus on the
poorest ones.

00:06:13.340 --> 00:06:20.360
This puts Transylvania in a very bad position,
and that’s because they are wealthier than

00:06:20.360 --> 00:06:23.949
the other regions...

00:06:23.949 --> 00:06:31.189
And this, well this, is how a new political
party was born: the Democratic Alliance of

00:06:31.189 --> 00:06:34.759
Hungarians of Romania, also known as the UDMR.

00:06:34.759 --> 00:06:39.860
Unsurprisingly, they won all the elections
in regions where Hungarians are the majority...

00:06:39.860 --> 00:06:42.139
So, what are their foundations?

00:06:42.139 --> 00:06:46.349
Basically, they claim Romania is sucking their
blood… and their money.

00:06:46.349 --> 00:06:49.259
Yes… it is the same as in the Catalonian
case!

00:06:49.259 --> 00:06:54.099
And their solution to end Romanian looting
is… imitating the fiscal model of another

00:06:54.099 --> 00:06:55.099
Spanish region: the BASQUE country.

00:06:55.099 --> 00:06:56.099
Let me explain to you what happens here for
a moment.

00:06:56.099 --> 00:06:57.099
The Basque Country is a region inside of Spain
with a very special tax system.

00:06:57.099 --> 00:07:00.819
Unlike the other regions, the Basque citizens
don’t pay their taxes to Madrid but to their

00:07:00.819 --> 00:07:02.460
local government instead.

00:07:02.460 --> 00:07:09.499
Once the money is collected, the local government
has to give some share to the central government.

00:07:09.499 --> 00:07:12.309
But the rest is to be managed the way the
local government wants…

00:07:12.309 --> 00:07:13.309
Alright, so back to Transylvania.

00:07:13.309 --> 00:07:17.159
So, this was the system proposed by the Szekelys
in 2014.

00:07:17.159 --> 00:07:19.229
And guess what the Romanian government replied…

00:07:19.229 --> 00:07:21.720
Well, they say it was against the constitution.

00:07:21.720 --> 00:07:26.639
The Romanian Constitution starts by saying
that that is a sovereign, unitary and in-di-vi-si-ble

00:07:26.639 --> 00:07:27.840
country.

00:07:27.840 --> 00:07:32.460
Of course, this created lots of protests in
different cities.

00:07:32.460 --> 00:07:36.729
There were referendum attempts and all sorts
of other symbolic objection...

00:07:36.729 --> 00:07:42.520
These are all things that hurt the Romanian
ruling class.

00:07:42.520 --> 00:07:49.719
ROMANIA’S RULING PARTY THREATENS AUTONOMY-SEEKING
TRANSYLVANIAN-HUNGARIANS WITH PRISON PUNISHMENT

00:07:49.719 --> 00:07:54.070
Attempts that threaten the constitutional
order of Romania should be punished with prison.

00:07:54.070 --> 00:07:58.070
If you’ve been following the case of the
Catalonian separatists, this might sound familiar

00:07:58.070 --> 00:07:59.070
to you...

00:07:59.070 --> 00:08:03.759
Well, hold on a second because the best is
still yet to come..

00:08:03.759 --> 00:08:06.809
AUTONOMY OR ANEXION?

00:08:06.809 --> 00:08:10.300
If anybody of you has ever been to Hungary,
I’m sure you might have seen someone wearing

00:08:10.300 --> 00:08:11.999
a T-Shirt with this map.

00:08:11.999 --> 00:08:16.150
It represents the shape of Hungary before
losing part of their territories before the

00:08:16.150 --> 00:08:20.849
World War I. Yes, even today, in the 21st
century, a lot of Hungarians keep dreaming

00:08:20.849 --> 00:08:23.550
about taking their old empire back.

00:08:23.550 --> 00:08:30.349
Among them there is their president, VIKTOR
ORBAN, the Vladimir Putin of the Danube.

00:08:30.349 --> 00:08:34.080
Just like the Russian President, Orban is
famous for prosecuting the journalists who

00:08:34.080 --> 00:08:35.750
dare to criticize him.

00:08:35.750 --> 00:08:39.620
He has passed anti gay-laws and wins elections
with over 60% the vote.

00:08:39.620 --> 00:08:44.720
And, of course, like every good ‘Putinist,’
Orban likes to rule not only his own country,

00:08:44.720 --> 00:08:46.380
but others too.

00:08:46.380 --> 00:08:49.230
“Orban supports the autonomy of the szekelis”

00:08:49.230 --> 00:08:51.269
OK, I know what you are thinking…

00:08:51.269 --> 00:08:55.490
Why does a President from another country
mess with the internal politics of another?

00:08:55.490 --> 00:09:00.350
At the end of the day, what the Szekelys want
is just to have more autonomy but… without

00:09:00.350 --> 00:09:01.350
leaving Romania, right?

00:09:01.350 --> 00:09:06.269
Well… in fact… those Szekely citizens
are also his citizens.

00:09:06.269 --> 00:09:10.320
Hungary Grants Citizenship Rights To Ethnic
Hungarians Abroad.

00:09:10.320 --> 00:09:11.550
Yep, you heard that right.

00:09:11.550 --> 00:09:16.370
All those Transylvanian-born Hungarians have
two passports, the right to study in Hungary

00:09:16.370 --> 00:09:19.280
and, of course, vote at Hungarian elections.

00:09:19.280 --> 00:09:22.000
This last thing is especially good for Orban.

00:09:22.000 --> 00:09:27.899
He is popular inside of Hungarian borders,
but outside, he absolutely steals the show...

00:09:27.899 --> 00:09:32.320
95% of Hungarians from abroad voted for his
party, the FIDESZ, at the latest legislative

00:09:32.320 --> 00:09:33.320
elections.

00:09:33.320 --> 00:09:36.690
Meanwhile, Romania considers those rights
for the Szekelys as a complete violation of

00:09:36.690 --> 00:09:39.690
their own sovereignty.

00:09:39.690 --> 00:09:45.769
In their opinion, if you vote in two different
countries, you can’t be loyal to the one

00:09:45.769 --> 00:09:46.940
where you live.

00:09:46.940 --> 00:09:52.950
All of this means the diplomatic relations
between Hungary and Romania are complicated...

00:09:52.950 --> 00:09:58.279
Thanks to this, Orban can use Romania as an
antagonist to his nationalist propaganda.

00:09:58.279 --> 00:10:01.980
And then Romania has a great chance to give
some Hungary some shit when it comes to European

00:10:01.980 --> 00:10:03.680
politics.

00:10:03.680 --> 00:10:07.860
And now you might be wondering…

00:10:07.860 --> 00:10:10.360
What does the European Union think about all
of this?

00:10:10.360 --> 00:10:14.449
The truth is that despite the Council of Europe
writing memorandums where they defend the

00:10:14.449 --> 00:10:17.620
rights of ethnic minorities, Brussels would
never let Hungary win.

00:10:17.620 --> 00:10:22.259
At the end of the day, Viktor Orban is like
Dracula, Frankenstein and Freddy Krueger of

00:10:22.259 --> 00:10:23.259
European politics.

00:10:23.259 --> 00:10:28.250
So, as long as things don’t turn ugly, don’t
expect any position from any EU institution

00:10:28.250 --> 00:10:32.880
or politician.

00:10:32.880 --> 00:10:35.270
But now this is your turn…

00:10:35.270 --> 00:10:38.620
Do you think Transylvania should have its
own autonomy?

00:10:38.620 --> 00:10:39.620
Or, perhaps, this is

00:10:39.620 --> 00:10:43.040
nothing by a attempt from Hungary to get back
its sway on their former territories?

